"stephen-lawrence","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sue Higginson","person_id":"nsw_2268","person_slug":"sue-higginson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Wes Fang","person_id":"nsw_2232","person_slug":"wes-fang","vote":"no"}],"name":"Industrial Relations and Other Legislation Amendment (Miscellaneous)  Bill 2026","noes":16,"question":"That is not an anti‑business proposition. We believe that workers in a business should work together with the owners and controllers of that business for better outcomes. The type of mentality that says it is somehow going to be terrible that employers, if they introduce new technology, would have to consult with their employees first, portrays employees as a class of ignoramuses who do not understand anything about their own jobs. It is a really silly way of looking at things. This is just consultation. Any good employer would already be consulting because they understand how valuable their employees are. The response to the amendments—which I would say most Labour members probably agree with—is an unfortunate way to devalue workers in businesses across this State. I commend the amendments to the Committee.","result":"negative","slug":"division-nsw-lc-2026-11-19-6","source_url":"https://api.parliament.nsw.gov.au/api/hansard/search/daily/fragment/HANSARD-1820781676-106797"}
